"Bueno, Property Finance Simplified\"></div>\n  <p class=\"kick\">This fortnight in Spanish property</p>\n  <p class=\"date\">The Bueno Newsletter</p>\n  <p class=\"hi\">It has been a big fortnight. Prices hit a new record, and the Supreme Court ruled on a community fee that many owners will recognise.</p>\n  <div class=\"story\"><p class=\"tag\">News</p><h4>Used home prices hit an all-time record.</h4><p>Used homes averaged 2,955 euros per square metre in October, the highest idealista has ever recorded.</p></div>\n  <div class=\"story\"><p class=\"tag\">News</p><h4>The Supreme Court strikes down a 50 cent a day late fee.</h4><p>Communities can still chase unpaid fees, but their penalties have to stay reasonable.</p></div>\n  <div class=\"guide\"><p class=\"tag\">Free guide</p><h4>Community fees in Spain: what you pay and your rights.</h4><p>What your fees pay for, how the yearly meeting works and how to challenge a decision.</p><span class=\"btn\">Read the guide</span></div>\n  <div class=\"story\"><p class=\"tag\">Region spotlight</p><h4>Marbella and the western Costa del Sol.</h4><p>The OECD has named the M&aacute;laga and Marbella area the hardest place in Spain to buy a home.</p></div>\n  <div class=\"story\"><p class=\"tag\">Reader&#39;s question</p><h4>&ldquo;Our community wants to fine owners who pay late. Are they allowed to?&rdquo;</h4><p>Yes, but the penalty has to be in proportion to what is owed.</p></div>\n  <p class=\"sign\">Until the next edition,<br><b>Maria, the Bueno Team</b></p>\n</div></div></div>\n  </div></div>\n  <div class=\"badge\"><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"t\">A two-minute read, every second Monday.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"cap\"><span>A look inside your inbox</span><span>Hover to pause</span></div>\n</div></div>\n", "appliedThemeId": null, "siteTemplateId": null}}]}]}]}, {"type": "section", "attrs": {"id": "0c84eab6-77e3-4dc8-9ca1-0bb8d639da28", "gap": "0", "align": "left", "color": "#000000FF", "width": "100dvh", "layo